<article class="env-lemma" id="0CZN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CZN">Lemma <span data-tag="0CZN">15.27.4</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $M$ be a finite $R$-module. Let $k \geq 0$ and $I = \text{Fit}_ k(M)$. Assume that $M_\mathfrak p$ is free of rank $k$ for every $\mathfrak p \not\in V(I)$. Then for every $a \in I$ with $R' = R[\frac{I}{a}]$ the strict transform </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  M' = (M \otimes _ R R')/a\text{-power torsion}  \]
</div>
  <p> is locally free of rank $k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0CZM" data-tag="0CZM">15.27.3</a> we have $\text{Fit}_ k(M') = R'$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZD" data-tag="07ZD">15.8.8</a> it suffices to show that $\text{Fit}_{k - 1}(M') = 0$. Recall that $R' \subset R'_ a = R_ a$, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/07Z3" data-tag="07Z3">10.70.2</a>. Hence it suffices to prove that $\text{Fit}_{k - 1}(M')$ maps to zero in $R'_ a = R_ a$. Since clearly $(M')_ a = M_ a$ this reduces us to showing that $\text{Fit}_{k - 1}(M_ a) = 0$ because formation of Fitting ideals commutes with base change according to Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZA" data-tag="07ZA">15.8.4</a> part (3). This is true by our assumption that $M_ a$ is finite locally free of rank $k$ (see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00NX" data-tag="00NX">10.78.2</a>) and the already cited Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZD" data-tag="07ZD">15.8.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>